Subject: [202605] Wire Edgecore hardware watchdogs without query side effects

Add adapters for the native AS5835 API and PDDF AS7326/AS7726/AS7816.
Use the common platform package (already required by all four APIs),
rather than forcing native AS5835 into PDDF mode. Fix the missing syslog
import exposed by missing platform adapters in PR #25049.
Avoid the existing generic PDDF watchdog constructor: it opens/arms and
disables hardware even for status, and an already inactive disarm fails.
The new adapter discovers supported identities through sysfs, uses
four-byte ioctl arguments and the driver-returned timeout, reads kernel
state across processes, and treats repeated disarm as success. Explicit
arm/disarm still require controlled hardware validation per model.
References: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/25049
https://docs.kernel.org/watchdog/watchdog-api.html

Verified source: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.
Remove individual fixes when upstream supplies equivalent behavior.
Software regressions cover these changes; only AS7326 has been
inspected live. Other models require installation/hardware validation.

